## For Further Study

- **{{symbol:wings}}** — The covenant term that pairs most frequently with shadow; four psalms layer both terms together to describe divine shelter.
- **{{symbol:booths}}** — The appointed time of Sukkot is the enacted shadow: {{ref:Isa.4.6}} tabernacle for a shadow = {{ref:Col.2.17}} appointed times as shadow, constructed from {{symbol:myrtle}} branches.
- **{{symbol:myrtle}}** — The faithful remnant dwelling in the shade ({{ref:Zech.1.8}}); the anti-thorn that replaces the cursed order and becomes the material of God's shelter.
- **{{symbol:rock}}** — The covenant body that casts the shadow in {{ref:Isa.32.2}}; traces the identity of the "great rock" across Scripture.
